WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.200
Agenitc development is powerful, but scaling what one person can do

2
00:00:04.200 --> 00:00:08.920
on their laptop to a repeatable process across your team and large code bases...

3
00:00:09.040 --> 00:00:10.080
that gets tricky.

4
00:00:10.080 --> 00:00:13.120
In this upcoming webinar, we'll talk about common failure scenarios

5
00:00:13.120 --> 00:00:16.160
when scaling agentic development and what can you do about them.

6
00:00:16.160 --> 00:00:19.160
Spoiler alert: a lot of that comes down to context.

7
00:00:19.160 --> 00:00:22.600
We’ll mention common use cases for context, like rolling out

8
00:00:22.600 --> 00:00:25.600
policies and best practices or documenting your platform,

9
00:00:25.800 --> 00:00:29.000
and we will discuss how the context development lifecycle

10
00:00:29.000 --> 00:00:32.440
connects to the software development lifecycle and how it can scale.

11
00:00:32.880 --> 00:00:35.240
If that sounds interesting, follow the link to register.

12
00:00:35.240 --> 00:00:36.040
I hope to see you there.
